Symptoms of shock can include rapid heartbeat, weak pulse, shallow breathing, cold and clammy skin, confusion or loss of consciousness, and a drop in blood pressure. These signs indicate an inadequate blood flow to organs and tissues, which can lead to severe complications if not promptly treated. Other symptoms may include anxiety, restlessness, and enlarged pupils. It is crucial to seek immediate medical assistance when experiencing these symptoms.
